// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna - Legacy of the Phanerozoic: Carnivorous Bull (abelisauridae).
//
// Eighteen abelisaurids, from a 3.4 tonne Pycnonemosaurus down to a 250 kg Tarascosaurus, plus their
// nests. Same authors and same shape as the Birds of Prey raptors, and the same one real problem.
//
// 1. PREY NEEDS NO RESCUING. The mod writes a proper hunt list - wild pigs, gazelle, deer, horses,
//    and the other Legacy of the Phanerozoic herbivore groups (pachycephalosaurs, ankylosaurs,
//    ceratopsians, ornithomimosaurs, sauropods, stegosaurs, therizinosaurs, hadrosaurs) - gated on
//    whenNotInEmotionState "saturated", which is to say hunt when not full. A SECOND list of rival
//    predators (wolves, bears, big cats, other theropods, and abelisaurids themselves) is gated on
//    "aggressiveondamage", so it reads as retaliation and never becomes a food supply. That is a
//    well-made distinction and Cycle of Life honours it as written.
//
//    MASS BANDS are set anyway: the hunt list names sibling mods a given server may not have
//    installed, and a band reaches whatever herbivores actually are present instead. Upper bounds
//    run to about twice body mass, which is what a large theropod taking ornithischians implies
//    without pretending a lone Carnotaurus pulls down a full-grown sauropod.
//
// 2. BODY WEIGHT, DECLARED AS A FLAT 4000 kg FOR EVERY ADULT. Too heavy for all eighteen, and by
//    more than tenfold at the small end. Weight drives forage demand, grazing range, territory
//    radius and the satiation reserve here, so this is the correction that matters. Masses are
//    published estimates, mid-range where sources disagree.
//
//    Where the fossil record is thin - Thanos is a single vertebra, Tarascosaurus and Dahalokely
//    little better - the mod own hitbox ordering is used as the tiebreak, since it is at least the
//    author stated intent. Where the record is good, it wins: Pycnonemosaurus and Carnotaurus share
//    a hitbox in the mod but not a mass, because a 3.4 tonne animal and a 1.5 tonne one are not the
//    same animal however they are drawn.
//
// NESTS ARE CHAIN SEEDS, as in the raptor file: they carry "bellalarm" beside "idle" so they fail
// the static test and would otherwise be managed as breeding animals. Only INCUBATING nests need
// entries - mature and empty get triesPerChunk 0. Eggs are runtime chance 0.0, and the lure and
// hitch have no spawn conditions at all, being player equipment.
//
// Lifespans are anchored on Majungasaurus, which has the best growth record in the family: slow
// maturity and a long life, scaled by size across the rest.
//
// VERIFICATION STATUS: keys derived from the mod own entity JSON, not read off a live roster - this
// mod is not installed on the pack author server. A wrong key is inert (the entry is ignored and the
// animal keeps its auto-discovered values); `/col species` lists the authoritative keys.
